(a) Designated. Immediately after the biennial organization of the city council, the mayor shall appoint the following standing committees and chairmen thereof:
(1) Fire and EMS;
(2) Personnel, finance and administration;
(3) Police;
(4) Public works;
(5) Recreation;
(6) Water and sewage; and
(7) Zoning and building.
(b) Membership; powers and duties of chairmen.
(1) All standing committees of the council shall consist of a membership of not less than three members of the council. The mayor shall appoint the members to each committee.
(2) It shall be the duty of the chairman of each committee to preside at all meetings of the committee, and his committee shall be subject to his call for meetings. It shall be the duty of the chairman to report the recommendations and findings of his committee or a majority finding to the council at each regular session of the council. No chairman of a committee shall have the power or authority to make any recommendation or take any action on any matter without the agreement thereto of a majority of his committee, the chairman being entitled to vote with other members of the committee on any question.
(Code 1976, §§ 2-1061, 2-1062)

